  "footnotes": [],
  "context": "Section 137 on medical practice uses this table to show the hospitals, qualified physicians, Japanese permitted to practise, Chinese-school Korean practitioners, pharmacists, midwives and nurses in each province at the end of 1911.",
  "transcriber_notes": [
   "Rows: 14 provinces/locations plus Total as printed (15).",
   "Dashes in original written as \"—\".",
   "Keijō row, Hospitals Private Japanese: read 46 (4 partly covered by an ink smudge in the scan, glyph still legible as 4).",
   "South Keishō row, Qualified Physicians Total: bold glyph blotted, 3-vs-8 rule applied: 97+—+1=98 reconciles only with 8, so 98.",
   "Column sums of the 14 rows match the printed Total row for every column except Nurses: rows sum to 333, printed total 337 (as printed; every Nurses cell re-read, none doubtful).",
   "Row checks: Hospitals Total = Government + Public Corporation + Private Total, and Physicians Total = Japanese+Korean+Foreign, hold for every row.",
   "Verified: an independent blind second transcription agreed on every other cell; the totals that do not reconcile are as printed."
